From: rodman80 <rodman80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Nov 2026 13:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] O(queries x routes) q4 prefill slice planner behind
 VLLM_EXL3_Q4KV_PLANNER_V2

plan_prefill_slices_fast partitions a prefill chunk's queries into runs whose selected-page
union fits the 48 MiB staging buffer (384 pages per rank at 2 KV heads). When one request's
own union exceeds the cap it builds a [rows, nb] page bitmap and, for EVERY slice start a,
calls _union_curve(a) -> _first_row_at_or_after(a): an [(rows - a), nb] int64 where/amin.
nb is the PHYSICAL pool size, not the prompt length: at KVB=20 GB per rank over 60 layers
that is 9,042 pages, so one call is 1.1 GiB and a long-context chunk needs 6-40 of them.

Measured on GB10 at the served geometry (kernel-lab/results/a3_planner.json), 16K-token
chunk: plan 69.8 ms -> 2.57 ms per layer over a 192K prefix (27x), 43.5 -> 2.2 ms at 48K
(20x), and the whole prefill sparse-attention operation 4.3x / 3.5x / 5.8x at 192K / 48K /
112K prefixes. At a prefix of 0 the request's union fits the cap, the per-query path is
never entered, and the change is neutral (10.07 -> 10.05 ms).

cov(a+k) = #{page : first[page] < a+k} is nondecreasing in k, so the greedy's answer -- the
largest k with cov(a+k) <= cap -- is exactly first_sorted[cap] - a: one ascending sort of nb
elements per slice, and the slice's page list is what that sort already ordered. No
[rows, nb] tensor is built.

Same greedy, same maximal ranges, same hard floor, same ascending page order, same -1
handling. Host transfers go from one per slice (the reference's searchsorted(...).tolist())
to two device scalars per slice -- O(slices) either way, never O(slices x rows), and the
plan is unaffected. The plan and every page list are identical to the reference planner
(tests/test_q4kv_slice_planner.py), so the staged bf16 bytes and the attention output are
bit-identical. Default OFF: unset selects the reference planner byte for byte; a malformed
value raises rather than silently selecting a path.

Part of the plugin series (config/pins.sh PATCH_FILES), so it is in both the pack-builder
and the serve image. The serve env sets VLLM_EXL3_Q4KV_PLANNER_V2=1 (m31.sh); unsetting it
returns the pre-0020 code path byte for byte with no rebuild, which is the rollback. The
Dockerfile self-checks assert slice_planner.py exists, that it defines
plan_prefill_slices_v2, and that the switch is present in minimax_q4kv.py. Plan equality is
checked against the reference planner by tests/test_q4kv_slice_planner.py in this lane.
